		<!--
			The affinity note, OUTSIDE the box it explains and directly under it (SPEC I134d, T898,
			user 2026-09-02: "deve ficar fora do box, em baixo do box").

			It has moved twice for the same reason and this is the third address. It rode the right
			end of hedgeStrip until T830 took the strip; T830 put it INSIDE the box, in the foot the
			column had just gained. Inside, it read as a twenty-first ROW of a list of twenty - which
			is what the user is asking to undo, and the 25px of foot the box carried for it is what
			made the column 586 against the 561 of PSYCHIC PHENOMENA beside it. Out here the two
			columns close on ONE y, which is the shape they always should have had.

			left=491 and not 471: it lines up with the ROWS of the box above, not with the box edge,
			so the caption and the list it captions share one left. width 426 is the row width, and
			top is derived - the box opens at 151 and is 561 tall, and 5 is the gutter V298 rules
			between two things stacked on this sheet.

			Still a bare label: it carries no field and no rectangle, so V40 and V48 - which measure
			BOXES - have nothing to say about it out here either, and the V280/V298 collectors walk
			<layout> nodes carrying a <rectangle> and never see it (MEASURED, not assumed).
		-->
		<label name="noteHedgePaths" left="491" top="702" width="426" height="20" text="* The first path is the Affinity Path" fontSize="12" vertTextAlign="center"/>
	</scrollBox>

	<!--
		One link for the whole tab, and it watches what the PAINTER reads (SPEC V123): the
		sixty rows whose buttons carry their value - numina_1..20, psychic_1..15 and 20..24
		(16..19 are the burned PSYCHIC_VACANT) and hedgeRitual_1..20, the bounds
		renderNuminaButtons walks - and the language they carry it in. A button's text is not
		data, so nothing else brings it back after an open or a change (SPEC I107a2, V383a).
		The list stopped at numina_15, psychic_15 and hedgeRitual_12 while the painters walked
		to the constants, so a pick on the rows past those never repainted until the tab was
		reopened (SPEC B209, 101st batch).

		numinaSel, psychicSel and hedgeRitualSel left the list with the panes - nothing reads a
		marked row any more (SPEC V365d, user 2026-08-31). The faith field left in the 90th round and has
		not come back: the True Faith ? opens on a fixed key, so the religion beside it drives
		nothing (SPEC I61, V265).
	-->
	<dataLink fields="{'language', 'hedgeAffiliation', 'numina_1', 'numina_2', 'numina_3', 'numina_4', 'numina_5', 'numina_6', 'numina_7', 'numina_8', 'numina_9', 'numina_10', 'numina_11', 'numina_12', 'numina_13', 'numina_14', 'numina_15', 'numina_16', 'numina_17', 'numina_18', 'numina_19', 'numina_20', 'psychic_1', 'psychic_2', 'psychic_3', 'psychic_4', 'psychic_5', 'psychic_6', 'psychic_7', 'psychic_8', 'psychic_9', 'psychic_10', 'psychic_11', 'psychic_12', 'psychic_13', 'psychic_14', 'psychic_15', 'psychic_20', 'psychic_21', 'psychic_22', 'psychic_23', 'psychic_24', 'hedgeRitual_1', 'hedgeRitual_2', 'hedgeRitual_3', 'hedgeRitual_4', 'hedgeRitual_5', 'hedgeRitual_6', 'hedgeRitual_7', 'hedgeRitual_8', 'hedgeRitual_9', 'hedgeRitual_10', 'hedgeRitual_11', 'hedgeRitual_12', 'hedgeRitual_13', 'hedgeRitual_14', 'hedgeRitual_15', 'hedgeRitual_16', 'hedgeRitual_17', 'hedgeRitual_18', 'hedgeRitual_19', 'hedgeRitual_20'}" onChange="renderNuminaButtons(self);"/>
	<!-- The picked rituals wear their level in art, so the art follows the row (SPEC I65). It
	     is a link of its own and not more handlers on the one above: that one repaints the row
	     labels and their buttons, and a level is neither. All twenty rows and the five dot
	     fields of each - it stopped at hedgeRitual_17, so rows 18-20 kept stale dots (SPEC B209). -->
	<dataLink fields="{'hedgeRitual_1', 'hedgeRitual_2', 'hedgeRitual_3', 'hedgeRitual_4', 'hedgeRitual_5', 'hedgeRitual_6', 'hedgeRitual_7', 'hedgeRitual_8', 'hedgeRitual_9', 'hedgeRitual_10', 'hedgeRitual_11', 'hedgeRitual_12', 'hedgeRitual_13', 'hedgeRitual_14', 'hedgeRitual_15', 'hedgeRitual_16', 'hedgeRitual_17', 'hedgeRitual_18', 'hedgeRitual_19', 'hedgeRitual_20', 'hedgeRitual_1_1', 'hedgeRitual_1_2', 'hedgeRitual_1_3', 'hedgeRitual_1_4', 'hedgeRitual_1_5', 'hedgeRitual_2_1', 'hedgeRitual_2_2', 'hedgeRitual_2_3', 'hedgeRitual_2_4', 'hedgeRitual_2_5', 'hedgeRitual_3_1', 'hedgeRitual_3_2', 'hedgeRitual_3_3', 'hedgeRitual_3_4', 'hedgeRitual_3_5', 'hedgeRitual_4_1', 'hedgeRitual_4_2', 'hedgeRitual_4_3', 'hedgeRitual_4_4', 'hedgeRitual_4_5', 'hedgeRitual_5_1', 'hedgeRitual_5_2', 'hedgeRitual_5_3', 'hedgeRitual_5_4', 'hedgeRitual_5_5', 'hedgeRitual_6_1', 'hedgeRitual_6_2', 'hedgeRitual_6_3', 'hedgeRitual_6_4', 'hedgeRitual_6_5', 'hedgeRitual_7_1', 'hedgeRitual_7_2', 'hedgeRitual_7_3', 'hedgeRitual_7_4', 'hedgeRitual_7_5', 'hedgeRitual_8_1', 'hedgeRitual_8_2', 'hedgeRitual_8_3', 'hedgeRitual_8_4', 'hedgeRitual_8_5', 'hedgeRitual_9_1', 'hedgeRitual_9_2', 'hedgeRitual_9_3', 'hedgeRitual_9_4', 'hedgeRitual_9_5', 'hedgeRitual_10_1', 'hedgeRitual_10_2', 'hedgeRitual_10_3', 'hedgeRitual_10_4', 'hedgeRitual_10_5', 'hedgeRitual_11_1', 'hedgeRitual_11_2', 'hedgeRitual_11_3', 'hedgeRitual_11_4', 'hedgeRitual_11_5', 'hedgeRitual_12_1', 'hedgeRitual_12_2', 'hedgeRitual_12_3', 'hedgeRitual_12_4', 'hedgeRitual_12_5', 'hedgeRitual_13_1', 'hedgeRitual_13_2', 'hedgeRitual_13_3', 'hedgeRitual_13_4', 'hedgeRitual_13_5', 'hedgeRitual_14_1', 'hedgeRitual_14_2', 'hedgeRitual_14_3', 'hedgeRitual_14_4', 'hedgeRitual_14_5', 'hedgeRitual_15_1', 'hedgeRitual_15_2', 'hedgeRitual_15_3', 'hedgeRitual_15_4', 'hedgeRitual_15_5', 'hedgeRitual_16_1', 'hedgeRitual_16_2', 'hedgeRitual_16_3', 'hedgeRitual_16_4', 'hedgeRitual_16_5', 'hedgeRitual_17_1', 'hedgeRitual_17_2', 'hedgeRitual_17_3', 'hedgeRitual_17_4', 'hedgeRitual_17_5', 'hedgeRitual_18_1', 'hedgeRitual_18_2', 'hedgeRitual_18_3', 'hedgeRitual_18_4', 'hedgeRitual_18_5', 'hedgeRitual_19_1', 'hedgeRitual_19_2', 'hedgeRitual_19_3', 'hedgeRitual_19_4', 'hedgeRitual_19_5', 'hedgeRitual_20_1', 'hedgeRitual_20_2', 'hedgeRitual_20_3', 'hedgeRitual_20_4', 'hedgeRitual_20_5'}" onChange="paintHedgeRitualDots(self);"/>


	<!-- The affiliation decides what the Affinity Path row and the casting attribute may offer,
	     so the two lists are rebuilt when it changes (SPEC I67, I68, V272d). A link of its own
	     and not another field on the description one above: that one parses the book for three
	     text blocks, and an affiliation is not a description (SPEC V206).

	     At form level like every other dataLink on this sheet, not inside the HEDGE MAGIC box:
	     there are twenty-odd links across the fifteen forms and not one of them is nested, and
	     the handler walks up from `self` anyway (SPEC V143). -->
	<!-- The EXPERIENCE box of this tab follows a purchase made on ANY tab (SPEC I11, V133). -->
	<dataLink field="xpTotal" onChange="renderXPBoxes(self);"/>
	<dataLink field="hedgeAffiliation" onChange="renderHedgePickers(self);"/>

	<!-- The storyteller flag that swaps this tab's Affiliation picker for a typed field
	     (SPEC I71, V274). It is wired where the control it swaps lives, the same place the
	     clan-discipline lock is wired (SPEC V175) - the flag is set two tabs away and every
	     client at the table has to follow it, not just the one that ticked it. -->
	<dataLink field="stManualAffiliation" onChange="renderManualEntry(self);"/>

	<!-- Second, independent entry point: the blocks must be filled when the reader can SEE them,
	     not only after they touch something. It used to hang on onNodeReady and cite SPEC
	     V19 / V33 for it - but neither invariant asks for paint at OPEN: V19 forbids a silent
	     `if ~= nil` init path and V33 demands explicit state text for an unresolved row. The
	     comment was reading more into them than they say (SPEC I26), and onNodeReady fires on
	     every open, dragging the whole 380 KB module in with it (SPEC B47). onShow costs
	     nothing until the tab is actually visited.

-->
	<event name="onShow">
		wodTrace("WoD20.7.onShow");
		renderXPBoxes(self);
		renderHedgePickers(self);
		renderManualEntry(self);
		renderNuminaButtons(self);
		paintHedgeRitualDots(self);
	</event>
</form>
